    "updated_at": "2023-10-15T05:16:29Z",
    "body": "This is well-specified [here](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#reflecting-content-attributes-in-idl-attributes), under the \"If a [reflected IDL attribute](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#reflected-idl-attribute) has the type [USVString](https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#idl-DOMString)\" case. It has nothing to do with `about:blank` documents in particular, just about URL parsing: [parsing /foo against about:blank results in a parse failure](https://jsdom.github.io/whatwg-url/#url=L2Zvbw==&base=YWJvdXQ6Ymxhbms=). Because the result of step 4.2 is failure, we fall back to step 5, so Firefox and Safari's behavior is correct.\r\n\r\nIn particular, this means the bug is in Chromium's `URL` reflected attribute thing. <del>This maybe the source of some of [Chrome's Interop 2023 failures on URLs](https://wpt.fyi/results/url/a-element.html%3Fexclude%3D(file%7Cjavascript%7Cmailto)?label=experimental&label=master&aligned). /cc @hayatoito</del> <ins>No, nevermind, `HTMLAnchorElement` does not use `[Reflect, URL]` in this way.</ins>\r\n\r\nI hope this helps!",
